  (fn-do _ read-step Typed
    (param loop SyntaxId)
    (param slot SlotId)
    (param type TypeId)
    (param done IRBlockId)
    ; One pass of a loop whose header is a grammar, as the reference makes it: the stream
    ; kept for the loop is asked whether it has more, and the loop ends where it has not; it
    ; gives its view, and the pattern is matched from where the view starts, as a rule's arms
    ; are, without reading the rest, asking the stream for more input where a part reads past
    ; the end of its buffer. Where it passes, the stream commits where it ended, and the item is
    ; what it gives; where it fails, the stream commits where it started, and the loop ends.
    ; Where it passed without moving the stream on, it panics, as a pipe does. The names it
    ; captures stay bound for the body.
